course: dictionary
lesson: 7666
title: Words that push forward
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Propel means to push or drive something forward. A car is propelled by its engine, and a boat is propelled by its oars. When you meet propel in a text, ask: what is doing the pushing or driving?
explain: In «a self-propelling man-of-war with the armour-plated upper deck» (a warship with armour on top), self-propelling means the ship moves by its own power, with nobody pushing it from outside. You can test this by swapping in your own meaning: a ship that drives itself still makes sense.
explain: Propel can also mean to send someone into a new situation. A character can be propelled by fear or anger, so fear or anger pushes them into doing something. «Her first song propelled her to fame» means the song suddenly made her famous.
fact: Propel is a verb: propel, propels, propelled, propelling.
fact: «Propel» means to push or drive something forward.
fact: «Self-propelled» means moving by its own power, with no one pushing it.
fact: «Jet-propelled» means driven forward by a jet of air or gas.
fact: A person can be «propelled» by a feeling, such as fear or anger, into doing something.
exercise: «The engine propelled the car down the road.» What does propelled mean here? | Stopped suddenly | Whistled loudly | *Pushed or drove forward | Painted bright red
exercise: Which of these is propelled by oars? | A pencil | *A boat | A cloud | A rock
exercise: Nadia writes, «Fear propelled her into action.» What does this suggest? | She was sleeping soundly | She forgot her fear straight away | She was too scared to move at all | *Fear pushed her into doing something
test: «The jet of air propels the balloon rocket across the room.» What does propels mean? | Stays still | *Pushes forward | Floats gently down | Pops and bursts
test: Which word is the past tense of propel? | propels | *propelled | propelling | propel
exam: «The singer's first song propelled her to fame.» What does propelled to fame mean? | *Sent suddenly into being famous | Stopped singing for good | Forced to hide from everyone | Lost her voice for a year
